Issue
Virtual Center is running 4.0, update 1.

Virtual Center crashes as soon as a host is added. The vpxd log shows:


.
.
.
[2010-08-26 15:38:13.711 07108 warning 'App'] [VpxdMoHost::GetLinkedVmInt] Getting linked vm for vmid 11 on host 10.0.2.121 - COULD NOT FIND IT    
[2010-08-26 15:38:13.727 07108 error 'App'] [VdbRecord] ExecuteQueryAndFetchResult SQLFetch failed. Error code = 100    
[2010-08-26 15:38:13.727 07108 error 'App'] [VdbRecord] ExecuteQueryAndFetchResult SQLFetch failed. Error code = 100    
[2010-08-26 15:38:13.899 07108 error 'App'] Win32 exception: Stack overflow (0xc00000fd)    [2010-08-26 15:38:13.899 07108 error 'App'] eip: 0x4e6067 esp: 0x56b4bcc ebp: 0x56b4be4    
[2010-08-26 15:38:13.899 07108 error 'App'] eax: 0x56b2000 ebx: 00000000 ecx: 0x56b2bc4 edx: 0xfffffffe edi: 0x3e1eec8 esi: 0x3e1eed8    

Solution
One of the reasons this can happen is if a VM that is running on the host has a large number of snapshots associated with it. For example a VM with 32 snapshots.

Commit all the snapshots. Add the host to the virtual center.

